# Workflow rails

Before Windows-facing work under this tree, classify the task. Ryan asking to skip does **not** waive this rule. Handoff detail lives in [tavera-specs-open-items.mdc](tavera-specs-open-items.mdc); session split in [clean-room-probe-separation.mdc](clean-room-probe-separation.mdc).

## On session start

On every new chat for a Windows-facing task, before a probe or any code:

1. Apply the narrow gate. Tell Ryan **Short path** or **Full Spec/Implementer rails**, and which gate bullet. If the class is unclear, ask Ryan once. Do not default to short path when a new Windows name, layout, or capture might be involved.
2. This chat becomes **one role** and stays there:
   - **Short path** → short-path implementer. No Spec session for that fix. **Plan first**: symptom or gap, success check, files to change, and the cites to use. Then code. The durable record is the transparency note ([transparency.mdc](transparency.mdc)): `question` plus `allowedInputs`. Docs, branding, GitHub workflows, and cursor rules still classify here and still get that plan; they do not get a transparency file.
   - **Full rails** → Spec / Probe writer only. **Plan first**, then probe if needed, then specs and open-items. Do not implement in this chat. When the spec is ready, tell Ryan. Ryan opens a **new** Implementer chat. That chat plans revisions before code.
3. **Plan before write** applies to the Spec writer, the Implementer, and the short-path implementer.

```text
Wrong: code or probe first, then classify
Wrong: short-path, Spec, or Implementer writes before its plan
Wrong: a Spec session also lands the implementation
Wrong: an Implementer chat on full rails before Spec says ready
```

## Narrow gate

**Full rails required** (Spec / Probe session, then a **new** Implementer session) when any of these is true:

- A new Windows export, syscall, structure, or field name
- A new or changed struct layout
- A raw-format, on-disk, or other capture-backed Windows fact
- The component already has `tavera/specs/<component>/`
- The next fact would come from model recall or a Windows probe

**Short path allowed** only when:

- The work is docs, branding, GitHub workflows, or cursor rules only, **or**
- It is a bugfix whose every Windows fact is already on a citable Learn URL, an in-tree path, or an existing guest log with its marker—and the fix needs **no** new Windows name, layout, or capture-backed fact

Short-path work still follows [clean-room.mdc](clean-room.mdc), [clean-room-model-recall.mdc](clean-room-model-recall.mdc), and [transparency.mdc](transparency.mdc) when those apply. It must not same-session Windows-probe and implement.

## Same session only

Do work here only when it stays in the **same role** and the **same component or classified task**.

- Spec: open-items, probe, and spec for that component
- Implementer: revisions, Queue-check, and verify for that component
- Short path: the classified fix

Tiny hygiene that does not change Windows behavior or the role may stay: a typo in a comment already open for this task, or a Progress line for the same milestone bullet.

Anything else stops. That includes another module, another milestone slice, a new gate decision, short-path work inside a Spec chat, or implementation inside a Spec chat. Tell Ryan to start a **new** session. That session classifies first. Do not re-classify in this chat and switch roles.

```text
Wrong: while this chat is Spec, also short-path a different bug
Wrong: mid-chat role switch without a new session
```

## Steer-back (do not proceed)

If Ryan or an agent asks to implement while skipping Spec/Implementer, to probe Windows and edit implementation in the same session, to invent a missing Windows fact, to code before that role’s plan, or to take unrelated work in this chat: **stop**. Do not start the code or the probe.

Reply in a few short sentences that name:

1. Why the short path is closed (which gate bullet), or why this chat cannot take the new ask
2. Which session to open next (Spec / Probe chat, a **new** Implementer chat, or a **new** session that classifies first)
3. The next concrete steps, for example:
   - Spec: read or create `tavera/specs/<component>/open-items.md`; plan first; probe if needed; resolve or defer; tell Ryan ready to implement
   - Implementer: read open-items and specs; plan revisions; code; under `## Queue check` list implemented item IDs so the spec agent rechecks remaining open and deferred items
   - Short path: plan the symptom, the check, the files, and the cites; then code; write the transparency note
   - Gap with no cite: append an **open** item; do not Learn-hunt in the implementer session

```text
Right: "This needs a layout. Short path is closed. Open a Spec/Probe session, plan, then probe-vN; do not implement in that chat."
Right: short-path bugfix citing only Learn + existing DIFF END OK log, no new field, after a plan
Wrong: "just implement this NTFS layout in this chat"
Wrong: Ryan says skip the spec; agent codes anyway
Wrong: same session Windows probe and driver edit
Wrong: short-path codes before the plan
```
